 "literal": "Beaten drum like are the base people themselves, because of carrying and telling to others the secrets they heard.",
 "translation": "The base are like a beaten drum, for they carry and blab to others every secret they happen to hear.",
 "modern": "கீழ்மக்கள் தாங்கள் கேட்ட இரகசியங்களைப் பிறரிடம் கொண்டுபோய்ச் சொல்வதால், அவர்கள் அடிக்கப்படும் பறை போன்றவர்கள் ஆவர்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet compares untrustworthy, base individuals to a beaten drum. A drum, when struck, loudly broadcasts its sound to everyone in the vicinity, keeping nothing to itself. Similarly, base people cannot contain any confidential information or secrets they happen to hear. They immediately carry and reveal these secrets to others, proving themselves completely incapable of maintaining trust.",
